    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d450">

                <pb facs="0853" n="757" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg757"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">881.00/1260</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Herrick</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi><anchor n="35" xml:id="d450-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-08-03"><hi rendition="#italic">August 3,
                        1926</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received August 13.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 6542</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my cable No. 305, August
                    3, 12 A.M.,<anchor n="36" xml:id="d450-f2"/> I have the honor to transmit
                    herewith a copy and translation of a Note dated July 29, 1926, from the Foreign
                    Office together with the text of the Memorandum concerning the Maritime
                    Surveillance of the Moroccan Coast from August 1, 1926.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Ambassador:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sheldon
                            Whitehouse</hi></signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Counselor of
                        Embassy</hi></closer>




                <xi:include href="d450-a1.xml" xpointer="d450-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d450-a2.xml" xpointer="d450-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d450-f1" n="35" type="source" xml:id="d450-f1-content">
                <p>The receipt of a similar note and memorandum from the Spanish Government was
                    reported in telegram No. 59 of Aug. 5, noon, from the Ambassador in Spain (not
                    printed). The following reply was sent Aug. 7, 3 p.m.: “38. Your 59, August 5,
                    noon. At your discretion you may remind the Spanish Government that the position
                    of this Government remains that set forth in the Department’s 43, July 31, 1925,
                    3 p.m. Kellogg.” (File No. 881.00/1257.) Department’s 43, July 31, 1925, not
                    printed, but see telegram No. 297, July 31, 1925, to the Ambassador in France,
                        <ref target="frus1925v02#pg_606"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                            Relations</hi>, 1925, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, p.
                        606</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d450-f2" n="36" xml:id="d450-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
